<title>EGYPT: Egypt sells off Cairo Sheraton at $147 mln.</title>
<headline>Egypt sells off Cairo Sheraton at $147 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Egypt state said on Tuesday it sold 100 percent of Cairo Sheraton Hotel Casino and Towers to one investor for 500 million pounds.</p>
<p>The five-star, 660-room hotel was sold as an asset to National Company for Tourist Projects, a wholly-owned Egyptian firm, securities sources told Reuters.</p>
<p>The hotel, operated by Sheraton Hotels Corp, is owned by the Egyptian-state holding National Tourism and Hotels. -- Cairo newsroom +20 2 5783290/1</p>
</text>
